 {
  "id": "hp-sec-body",
  "type": "section",
  "settings": { "style": "default", "width": "default", "padding": "large" },
  "style": { "bg": { "type": "none" } },
  "advanced": {},
  "children": [
   { "id": "hp-body-r1", "type": "row", "settings": {}, "style": {}, "advanced": {}, "children": [
    { "id": "hp-body-c1", "type": "column", "settings": { "width": "1-1" }, "style": {}, "advanced": {}, "children": [
     {
      "id": "hp-lead",
      "type": "text-block",
      "settings": {
       "preset": "editorial-serif",
       "content": "<p><em>A 1930s apartment that had been “modernised” one too many times — our job was to give it back its bones, and a lot of its warmth.</em></p>",
       "text_color": "var(--olo-color-text)",
       "font_size": "26",
       "line_height": "1.4",
       "text_align": "left",
       "max_width": "760"
      },
      "style": {},
      "advanced": {},
      "children": []
     },
     {
      "id": "hp-p1",
      "type": "text-block",
      "settings": {
       "content": "<p>We stripped away the laminate and dropped ceilings to find original parquet and generous proportions underneath. From there it was a careful rebuild: lime plaster walls, restored doors, and a palette pulled from the terracotta rooftops outside the window.</p>",
       "text_color": "var(--olo-color-text-muted)",
       "font_size": "18",
       "line_height": "1.75",
       "text_align": "left",
       "max_width": "760"
      },
      "style": {},
      "advanced": {},
      "children": []
     }
    ]}
   ]},
   { "id": "hp-body-split", "type": "row", "settings": { "gap": 14 }, "style": {}, "advanced": {}, "children": [
    { "id": "hp-split-c1", "type": "column", "settings": { "width": "1-2" }, "style": {}, "advanced": {}, "children": [
     {
      "id": "hp-split-img1",
      "type": "image",
      "settings": {
       "image_url": "",
       "media_bg": { "type": "solid", "color": "#e2d6c1" },
       "media_label": "before / structural",
       "image_width": "100%",
       "aspect_ratio": "4/3",
       "object_fit": "cover",
       "border_radius": "4"
      },
      "style": {},
      "advanced": {},
      "children": []
     }
    ]},
    { "id": "hp-split-c2", "type": "column", "settings": { "width": "1-2" }, "style": {}, "advanced": {}, "children": [
     {
      "id": "hp-split-img2",
      "type": "image",
      "settings": {
       "image_url": "",
       "media_bg": { "type": "solid", "color": "#e2d6c1" },
       "media_label": "after / finished",
       "image_width": "100%",
       "aspect_ratio": "4/3",
       "object_fit": "cover",
       "border_radius": "4"
      },
      "style": {},
      "advanced": {},
      "children": []
     }
    ]}
   ]},
   { "id": "hp-body-r2", "type": "row", "settings": {}, "style": {}, "advanced": {}, "children": [
    { "id": "hp-body-c2", "type": "column", "settings": { "width": "1-1" }, "style": {}, "advanced": {}, "children": [
     {
      "id": "hp-p2",
      "type": "text-block",
      "settings": {
       "content": "<p>The furniture is a mix of vintage finds and a few custom pieces — a long oak table built for actual dinners, a reading chair positioned for the afternoon light. Nothing too precious; everything meant to be used.</p>",
       "text_color": "var(--olo-color-text-muted)",
       "font_size": "18",
       "line_height": "1.75",
       "text_align": "left",
       "max_width": "760"
      },
      "style": {},
